<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2742" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antĕ-căpĭo</span></b> ,
			cēpi, ceptum, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to obtain before</i>,
				<i>to receive before.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: quam appellat
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόληψιν</span> Epicurus, anteceptam
			animo rei quandam informationem, <i>an inborn</i>, <i>innate idea</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 16, 43</span></i> B. and K. (cf. anticipatio,
			I.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To take possession of beforehand</i>, <i>to preoccupy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multa antecapere, quae bello usui forent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 32, 3</span></i>
			 Dietsch: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pontem anteceperat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 66</span></i>
			 Halm.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To anticipate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noctem antecapere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 55, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ea omnia luxu antecapere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 13, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
